Subject: [PATCH] OpenSSL: use OpenOrbis endian header

OpenOrbis provides the endian conversion macros required by OpenSSL
through <endian.h>, while its FreeBSD-compatible environment does not
provide <sys/endian.h>.

Keep the standard FreeBSD handling unchanged and select the OpenOrbis
header only when building against the OpenOrbis environment.

---
 include/openssl/byteorder.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/openssl/byteorder.h b/include/openssl/byteorder.h
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/include/openssl/byteorder.h
+++ b/include/openssl/byteorder.h
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
 #if defined(__OpenBSD__)
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #else
-#include <sys/endian.h>
+#include <endian.h>
 #endif
 #define OSSL_HTOBE16(x) htobe16(x)
 #define OSSL_HTOBE32(x) htobe32(x)
